        "biography": "Dorcas Wright\u00a0\"Dede\"\u00a0Gardner\u00a0(born October 16, 1967) is an American film producer. She has been president since the founding of\u00a0Plan B Entertainment\u00a0and has been serving as Co-President with\u00a0Jeremy Kleiner\u00a0since 2013.\u00a0She has won\u00a0Oscars\u00a0for producing the films\u00a012 Years a Slave (2013) and\u00a0Moonlight\u00a0(2016), becoming the first woman to win two Oscars for\u00a0Best Picture. She has also been nominated in the category for\u00a0The Tree of Life\u00a0(2011),\u00a0Selma (2014),\u00a0The Big Short\u00a0(2015),\u00a0Vice\u00a0(2018),\u00a0Women Talking\u00a0(2022), and\u00a0Nickel Boys\u00a0(2024).\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Colson Whitehead, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
